%erg 0.1
Title: erg new: say when DIR is no store and hint at reversed arguments
Created: 2026-11-09
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-11-09T11:42Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context
2026-11-09, while filing 0307, an agent typed `erg new tickets "Title"` (arguments reversed). The
binary then in use silently created a directory named after the title at the repo root, holding
`0001-tickets.erg`. Since #393 (0307) `erg new` refuses before creating anything, but its message
reads the title as a store to migrate: `new: Some title here has no .claims/ ... run: erg migrate
--claims Some title here (without the binary: mkdir Some title here/.claims ...)`. Following that
advice recreates the stray directory. Evidence bar: a user (here an agent) hit the friction.

## Design
In `cmdNew`, for an explicit DIR that does not exist (or is not a directory), refuse with
`new: no ticket store at DIR` instead of the claims message. When the title itself names a ticket
store (a directory holding `.claims/` or `NNNN-*.erg` files), add `-- arguments reversed? usage:
erg new TITLE [DIR]`. What `erg new` accepts does not change; nothing is created.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg new TITLE MISSING_DIR` exits 1, says "no ticket store", does not suggest migrate, creates nothing.
- [ ] `erg new STORE_DIR "Some title"` (reversed) exits 1 and the message says "arguments reversed".
- [ ] `make check` passes.
